From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hy310-tv: build the framebuffer from the source geometry, rebuild it on a change

Companion to 0107-media-drm-h713-follow-source-geometry.patch; applies with
-p1 from the project root (userspace/hy310-tv/main.c, README.md).

The framebuffer handed to the plane described the panel: CREATE_DUMB with the
CRTC mode's width and height, SRC_W/SRC_H the mode, and a check that refused
any source geometry other than the mode's (main.c, display_create_fb() and
evaluate()). In hdmi-ring mode that buffer carries nothing but format,
geometry and stride, and all three are the ring's -- which the firmware lays
out for the signal it detected (1280 byte lines at 720p, doku/nachtlog/E4).

Now the geometry comes from the capture device. evaluate() asks
QUERY_DV_TIMINGS as before (signal, timings) and then G_FMT (how the capture
lays the picture out); the framebuffer is built from G_FMT and rebuilt when it
changes, with the plane off in between: picture off, buffer new, picture on.
The off is deliberate -- the firmware mutes its output over its own
re-detection ("hdmirx set AV mute:1 1" first, "AV mute:0 0" last, doku/91
Punkt 2), and what stood on the wall while this program did nothing of the
kind was the old geometry's plane reading the new geometry's ring (A6-4).
SRC_W/SRC_H are the source's, CRTC_W/CRTC_H the panel's; 0107's atomic_check
accepts that in hdmi-ring mode and the composition behind the plane scales.

What the plane cannot do is said and the console stays: a source larger than
the panel, a width not divisible by 16, an odd height, and a timing the
driver refuses (-ERANGE: interlaced, or outside its cap) -- said once, not
per sample. bytesperline must equal the width (the plane programs the ring
stride from the pitch, and a dumb buffer is as wide as its pitch); anything
else is refused rather than approximated.

The startup line "offen ... Aufloesungswechsel ..." goes: the statement it made
about 0094 (a constant behind QUERY_DV_TIMINGS) is no longer true. What is
still open moves to the README: this program learns of a change only through
SOURCE_CHANGE, and whether the firmware fires it on a pure geometry change is
the measurement doku/91 Punkt 2.2 asks for. No second, polling detection is
built here for it.

Not measured: the whole path, on the board. This diff has been applied with
--dry-run against the tree and read against the V4L2/DRM API; it has not been
compiled (no build in this session).

